WEBVTT

NOTE Acme Corp, freight spend baseline. Thursday 10 September 2026. Speakers: Gil Thorne, Dana Whitlock, Sam Rivera.

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000
<v Gil Thorne>Sam, I've pulled last year's freight. Shall I give you the totals first?

00:00:07.500 --> 00:00:09.000
<v Sam Rivera>Please.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:19.000
<v Gil Thorne>We paid Cobalt nine hundred and twenty thousand euros last year, for four thousand four hundred and seventy pallets.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:24.000
<v Sam Rivera>About two hundred and six a pallet. How did it fall by quarter?

00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:36.000
<v Gil Thorne>Nine hundred and sixty in the first quarter, twelve hundred and ten in the second, twelve hundred and forty in the third, a thousand and sixty in the fourth.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:40.000
<v Sam Rivera>And by lane?

00:00:40.500 --> 00:00:49.000
<v Gil Thorne>Eighty-five percent on the southern lanes. The rest is mostly export loads, and a handful on the northern one.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:57.000
<v Gil Thorne>Fuel is a fixed surcharge, eleven percent on top of the base rate. It hasn't moved in two years.

00:00:57.500 --> 00:01:04.000
<v Dana Whitlock>Sorry I'm late. Is that the file Marta will be working from too?

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:10.000
<v Gil Thorne>Her side has the same invoices. She'll know these numbers better than we do.

00:01:10.500 --> 00:01:18.000
<v Dana Whitlock>Then I want to know them better than she does before the fifteenth. Sam, can you put them on one page for me?

00:01:18.500 --> 00:01:22.000
<v Sam Rivera>By Monday the fourteenth. Gil, can I have the file itself?

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:25.000
<v Gil Thorne>Tomorrow morning.
